# Testing & TDD Policy

Sales Enablement uses Vitest for the frontend and targeted Python tests for scripts and the Flask webhook. TDD is the default for new behavior.

## TDD flow

1. Write the failing test first. Confirm it fails for the intended reason.
2. Write the minimum code to pass.
3. Refactor with tests still green.
4. Wire the change end-to-end (see `no-scaffold-code.mdc`).
5. Update docs (see `documentation-maintenance.mdc`).

Skip TDD only for: trivial stylistic tweaks, pure docs changes, or when the user explicitly says "no TDD".

## Frontend (Vitest)

- Command: `pnpm test` from `superpatch-frontend/`.
- Tests live in `superpatch-frontend/src/__tests__/` — grouped by domain (e.g., `config-pathways.test.ts`, `canonical-ids-sync.test.ts`).
- Use Vitest + React Testing Library for component tests.
- Mock Supabase and external APIs with `vi.mock()`. Do not hit real APIs in tests.
- Required tests for new code:
  - Every new pure function gets at least one happy-path + one edge-case test.
  - Every new API route handler gets a request / response shape test.
  - Every new Edge Function gets a test harness that exercises the fetch path (can live in `_tests/` alongside the function).

## Cross-mirror tests (mandatory)

The canonical-ids-sync test asserts that `canonical_ids.json`, `src/lib/config/pathways.ts`, and `supabase/functions/_shared/pathways.ts` agree. Never weaken this test; if a new ID type is added (e.g., a new tool), extend the test to cover it.

## Python tests

- Flask webhook (`b2b_sales_enablement/appointment_webhook/`) — tests live alongside the module.
- Pathway scripts — smoke tests that assert `canonical_ids.json` loads and every referenced `contextual_file` exists.
- Run with `python -m pytest` from the script folder.

## Pre-merge verification

Before marking work complete:

- [ ] `pnpm test` from `superpatch-frontend/` — all green
- [ ] `pnpm tsc --noEmit` from `superpatch-frontend/` — no errors
- [ ] Python smoke checks pass for any touched scripts
- [ ] Linter clean on all changed files
- [ ] Doc delta appended per `documentation-maintenance.mdc`

## Rationalization prevention

| Excuse | Reality |
|---|---|
| "It's a one-line fix" | One-line fixes regress. Add the test. |
| "The behavior is obvious" | If it is obvious, the test is easy. Write it. |
| "I'll add tests in a follow-up" | Follow-ups never come. Test now. |
| "It's just wiring" | Wiring is where bugs hide. Test the wiring. |
| "I ran it manually" | Manual runs are not reproducible. Automate. |
